 #edb/ref 17592186048169 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049303 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049303 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049612 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049303 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049810 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049303 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050860 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049303 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186096665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049303 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186096666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049303 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186096667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049303 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186096668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049303 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428041 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186049303 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428042 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186049303 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428043 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186049303 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428044 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186049303 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428045 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186049303 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428046 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186049303 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428047 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186049303 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428048 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186049303 #edb/ref 1031 "Integration Using the Double-Angle Formulas" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049303 #edb/ref 1033 1038 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049303 #edb/ref 1034 1.054675984092879 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186049303 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "eae67b9f-eeff-516d-8910-5ef24609f9ed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050841 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049306 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050841 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133873 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050841 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133874 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050841 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133875 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050841 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428650 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050841 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428651 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050841 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428652 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050841 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428653 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050841 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428654 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050841 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428655 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050841 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428656 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050841 #edb/ref 1031 "Projecting Vectors Onto Subspaces in Inner Product Spaces" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050841 #edb/ref 1033 2126 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050841 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "6aced1c3-bd0e-5b1d-973e-105b955f9e1a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133576 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5548" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133576 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $V=\\mathbb{R}_2[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n\\langle {x}(t), {y}(t) \\rangle = x(1)y(1) + x(2)y(2) + x(3)y(3).\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector  $p(t) = 1 - t^2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133576 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "105a5a4a-2fea-54bb-97c6-c2a700b05f61" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133576 #edb/ref 1074 "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $\\langle \\cdot, \\cdot \\rangle$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${p}(t) = 1-t^2,$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(1)=0,\\qquad \np(2)= -3,\\qquad \np(3)=-8.\n$$\n\nComputing $\\|p(t)\\|$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(1)p(1)+p(2)p(2)+p(3)p(3)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(1)]^{2}+[p(2)]^{2}+[p(3)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(0)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(-8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+9+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{73}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133577 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5549" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133577 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $V=\\mathcal{C}\\left[0,1\\right]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $\\left[0,1\\right],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n\\langle x(t),y(t) \\rangle = \\displaystyle\\int_{0}^{1} x(t) y(t) \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $f(t)= 2t-1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133577 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5aafdd7d-939a-5690-ac4d-46b554524d75" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133577 #edb/ref 1074 "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $\\langle \\cdot, \\cdot \\rangle$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\| f(t)\\| = \\sqrt{\\langle  f(t),  f(t) \\rangle}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(f(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2t-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(4{t}^{2}-4t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{4{t}^{3}}{3}-2{t}^{2}+t)|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}-2+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\| f(t)\\| = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{1}{3}} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt 3}{3}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133578 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5550" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133578 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $V=\\mathcal{C}\\left[0,\\pi\\right]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $\\left[0,\\pi\\right],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n\\langle x(t),y(t) \\rangle = \\displaystyle\\int_{0}^{\\pi} x(t) y(t) \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nNormalize the vector $f(t)= 3t.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133578 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d279bb1d-754e-5044-9a01-d4c86f30b269" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133578 #edb/ref 1074 "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $\\langle \\cdot, \\cdot \\rangle$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\| f(t)\\| = \\sqrt{\\langle  f(t),  f(t) \\rangle}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{(3t)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }9{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{t}^{3}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =3{\\pi }^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\| f(t) \\|  = \\sqrt{3\\pi^3} = \\pi \\sqrt{3\\pi}.\n$$\n\nTo normalize the vector $f(t),$ we divide $f(t)$ by its norm $\\| f(t) \\| \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\frac{f(t)}{‖f(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi \\sqrt{3\\pi }}\\cdot 3t \\\\  & =\\frac{t\\sqrt{3}}{\\pi \\sqrt{\\pi }}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133629 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5908" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133629 #edb/ref 1071 "An inner product on $V = \\mathbb{R}^3$ is defined as $\\langle \\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y} \\rangle =  2x_1 y_1 + x_2 y_2 + 3x_3 y_3.$ \nCalculate the norm of the vector ![](images/59/596d25646a513272f62708b9370136c1ef45a120edee3a4454c1a559119be3e5.svg) under this inner product." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133629 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "35e7ce1a-b2cc-50dd-8bf7-24d20e55d623" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133629 #edb/ref 1074 "The norm of a vector $\\mathbf v$ with respect to an inner product $\\langle \\cdot, \\cdot \\rangle$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖=\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $\\|\\mathbf{v}\\|$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2\\cdot (3\\cdot 3)+2\\cdot 2+3\\cdot (1\\cdot 1)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18+4+3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133767 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186134401 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133767 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186134555 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133767 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272230 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133767 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272231 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133767 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186360801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133767 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186360802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133767 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186360803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921861